# The vocabulary a generated binding is written in.
#
# Curated by hand, rendered by `nts bind --members`. A hand-written prelude
# could be curated and could not carry a binding table: a table is numbered by
# byte offsets into the text, and a person cannot maintain those. This list is
# the half a person should write; the offsets come from the run that renders it.
#
# Named by the DECLARING class -- and that does not compose the way it looks
# like it should, because a Java interface redeclares what it inherits.
# `java.util.List` declares its own `size()`, so `Collection#size` does not put
# one on `List`. Being explicit per class is the honest form, and the compiler
# says which line is missing: `Property 'size' does not exist on type 'List'`.

java.util.Iterator#hasNext
java.util.Iterator#next

java.util.Collection#size
java.util.Collection#isEmpty
java.util.Collection#contains
java.util.Collection#iterator

java.util.List#size
java.util.List#isEmpty
java.util.List#contains
java.util.List#iterator
java.util.List#get
java.util.List#set
java.util.List#add
java.util.List#indexOf

java.util.Set#size
java.util.Set#isEmpty
java.util.Set#contains
java.util.Set#iterator

java.util.Map#size
java.util.Map#isEmpty
java.util.Map#get
java.util.Map#put
java.util.Map#containsKey
java.util.Map#remove
java.util.Map#keySet
java.util.Map#values

java.util.HashMap#<init>
java.util.HashMap#get
java.util.HashMap#put
java.util.HashMap#containsKey
java.util.HashMap#remove
java.util.HashMap#size
java.util.HashMap#isEmpty

java.lang.Number#intValue
java.lang.Number#longValue
java.lang.Number#doubleValue
java.lang.Integer#intValue
java.lang.Long#longValue
java.lang.Double#doubleValue
